{"text": "| ee a ee ee\n\nCHARGE NUMBE!\n\n2105\nPROGRAM TITLE: EXTRUDED FILTER DEVELOPMENT\nPERIOD COVERED: March 1 - March 31, 1972\nPROJECT LEADER: G. L. Mathe\nWRITTEN BY: J. F. Nienow\n\nDATE OF REPORT: April 5, 1972\n\nI. PROJECT TITLE: Extrusion Systems Development\n\nExtrusion line No. I has been run at 500 fpm for\nextended periods of time with only minor problems. This\nline is now undergoing extensive modification to increase\nits productivity. Among these modifications is a\nthermostatically controlled water chiller which has been\ninstalled and is working properly. The integration of the\ncutter and the conveyor into the line shaft! drive is now\nbeing designed and a new SH.P. D.C. drive has been purchased\nto motivate the new system. Driving the cutter from the line\nshaft should eliminate our current problem of cutting uniform\nYength at high speeds. The conveyor obtained for this system\nis a Molins Dual Action combiner part and will allow the fitting\nof an automatic tray filler at a later date.\n\nII. PROJECT TITLE: Foamed Plastic Filter Development\n\nThe Product Description and Process Manual has been\nwritten and is now being typed. No further work is scheduled\nexcept assistance to the Semi-Works on problems with ring\ntipping.\n\nIII. PROJECT TITLE: Non-Obvious Dilution Cigaret Development\n\nOver 4,000 cigarets were produced for a packaging\ntest. The test indicates no problems in handling the\nslightly raised tipping paper.* Current plans are for\na POL test around mid-April, a descriptive panel around\nthe latter part of April and SEF lab panel test in early\nMay. Further plans will depend on the results of these tests.\n\nSLESbIZz0z", "words": [{"text": "|", "x0": 14, "y0": 963, "x1": 25, "y1": 991, "conf": 32.0}, {"text": "ee", "x0": 16, "y0": 912, "x1": 25, "y1": 940, "conf": 34.0}, {"text": "a", "x0": 21, "y0": 860, "x1": 25, "y1": 888, "conf": 12.0}, {"text": "ee", "x0": 15, "y0": 658, "x1": 25, "y1": 787, "conf": 20.0}, {"text": "ee",